---
title: "outflow_limit - Borrow/Withdraw Outflow Rate Limiting (Scallop Lending)"
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> q_get_config: load outflow_limit config for asset T
    q_get_config --> q_get_window: window_duration = 24 hours, release_interval = 30 minutes

    q_get_window --> q_calc_released: for each past outflow entry
    q_calc_released --> q_check_expired: if entry.timestamp + 24h <= current_time
    q_check_expired --> q_release: entry expired, add back to available
    q_check_expired --> q_keep: entry still within window, remains consumed
    q_release --> q_calc_released: continue iteration
    q_keep --> q_calc_released: continue iteration

    q_calc_released --> q_calc_available: available_outflow = total_limit - sum(active_entries)
    q_calc_available --> q_check_request: requested_amount <= available_outflow

    q_check_request --> q_record: sufficient outflow available
    q_check_request --> q_error: outflow limit exceeded
    q_error --> [*]: revert (rate limit hit)

    q_record --> q_update: record new entry(amount, current_time)
    q_update --> [*]: outflow approved, continue with borrow/withdraw

    note right of q_get_window
        INV-001: outflow limit is per-asset and configurable
        INV-002: consumed outflow is released after 24 hours from consumption time
    end note

    note right of q_calc_available
        INV-003: available_outflow = total_limit - sum of non-expired outflow entries
        INV-004: 0 <= available_outflow <= total_limit at all times
    end note

    note right of q_record
        INV-005: outflow limit applies to both borrows and withdrawals
        INV-006: release happens gradually (every 30 minutes) not all at once
    end note
